.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_KDF-X963 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_KDF-X963
.Nd The X9.63-2001 EVP_KDF implementation
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The EVP_KDF-X963 algorithm implements the key derivation function
(X963KDF). X963KDF is used by Cryptographic Message Syntax (CMS) for EC
KeyAgreement, to derive a key using input such as a shared secret key
and shared info.
.Pp
The output is considered to be keying material.
.Ss Identity
"X963KDF" is the name for this implementation; it can be used with the
.Xr EVP_KDF_fetch 3
function.
.Ss Supported parameters
The supported parameters are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqproperties" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_PROPERTIES Ns ) <UTF8 string>
.It \(dqdigest" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_DIGEST Ns ) <UTF8 string>
These parameters work as described in
.Xr EVP_KDF 3 .
.It \(dqkey" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_KEY Ns ) <octet string>
The shared secret used for key derivation.
This parameter sets the secret.
.It \(dqinfo" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_INFO Ns ) <octet string>
This parameter specifies an optional value for shared info.
.El
.Pp
The OpenSSL FIPS provider also supports the following parameters:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqfips-indicator" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_FIPS_APPROVED_INDICATOR Ns ) <integer>
A getter that returns 1 if the operation is FIPS approved, or 0
otherwise.
This may be used after calling EVP_KDF_derive.
It returns 0 if any "***-check" related parameter is set to 0 and the
check fails.
.It \(dqdigest-check" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_FIPS_DIGEST_CHECK Ns ) <int>
The default value of 1 causes an error during
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_set_params 3
if used digest is not approved.
Setting this to zero will ignore the error and set the approved
"fips-indicator" to 0. This option breaks FIPS compliance if it causes
the approved "fips-indicator" to return 0.
.Pp
According to ANSI X9.63-2001, the following are approved digest
algorithms: SHA2-224, SHA2-256, SHA2-384, SHA2-512, SHA2-512/224,
SHA2-512/256, SHA3-224, SHA3-256, SHA3-384, SHA3-512.
.It \(dqkey-check" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_FIPS_KEY_CHECK Ns ) <integer>
The default value of 1 causes an error during
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_set_params 3
if the length of used key-derivation key
.Pf ( Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_KEY )
is shorter than 112 bits.
Setting this to zero will ignore the error and set the approved
"fips-indicator" to 0. This option breaks FIPS compliance if it causes
the approved "fips-indicator" to return 0.
.El
.Sh NOTES
X963KDF is very similar to the SSKDF that uses a digest as the auxiliary
function, X963KDF appends the counter to the secret, whereas SSKDF
prepends the counter.
.Pp
A context for X963KDF can be obtained by calling:
.Bd -literal
 EVP_KDF *kdf = EVP_KDF_fetch(NULL, "X963KDF", NULL);
 EVP_KDF_CTX *kctx = EVP_KDF_CTX_new(kdf);
.Ed
.Pp
The output length of an X963KDF is specified via the
.Em keylen
parameter to the
.Xr EVP_KDF_derive 3
function.
.Sh EXAMPLES
This example derives 10 bytes, with the secret key "secret" and
sharedinfo value "label":
.Bd -literal
 EVP_KDF *kdf;
 EVP_KDF_CTX *kctx;
 unsigned char out[10];
 OSSL_PARAM params[4], *p = params;

 kdf = EVP_KDF_fetch(NULL, "X963KDF", NULL);
 kctx = EVP_KDF_CTX_new(kdf);
 EVP_KDF_free(kdf);

 *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_utf8_string(OSSL_KDF_PARAM_DIGEST,
                                         SN_sha256, strlen(SN_sha256));
 *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_octet_string(OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SECRET,
                                          "secret", (size_t)6);
 *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_octet_string(OSSL_KDF_PARAM_INFO,
                                          "label", (size_t)5);
 *p = OSSL_PARAM_construct_end();
 if (EVP_KDF_derive(kctx, out, sizeof(out), params) <= 0) {
     error("EVP_KDF_derive");
 }

 EVP_KDF_CTX_free(kctx);
.Ed
.Sh CONFORMING TO
"SEC 1: Elliptic Curve Cryptography"
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_KDF 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_new 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_free 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_set_params 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_get_kdf_size 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF_derive 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF 3
